# python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0: udisks2 over D-Bus (Gio) on the command line.
# gir1.2-gtk-3.0: the window, GTK 3 so it follows the style's theme.
# udisks2: finds, mounts (read only) and unlocks the Windows disk; the
# kernel's ntfs3 reads NTFS, so ntfs-3g isn't needed.
# xdg-user-dirs: where Documents, Pictures and the rest are (xdg-user-dir).
# xdg-utils: Open Folder (xdg-open).
Depends: python3,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-glib-2.0,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         udisks2,
         xdg-user-dirs,
         xdg-utils,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: bring files over from a Windows disk to FlickOS
 Bring Files from Windows finds a Windows disk, in this computer, a second
 one or an old disk in a USB case, opens it read only and copies an
 account's Desktop, Documents, Downloads, Music, Pictures and Videos, and
 the same folders in OneDrive, into the matching folders at home. In the
 live session it copies to a USB drive, so files can be saved before
 Windows is erased.
 .
 Nothing on the Windows disk is changed. Files already there are never
 overwritten, Windows' own files and shortcuts are left out, and files that
 are only in OneDrive are listed with where to download them. Bookmarks
 from Chrome and Edge are saved as a file Firefox imports. Nothing runs in
 the background.
